git From ac1772e221c9dce9fe566c5710195ce8993a4f90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel <aloziefrompg@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:49:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mailchimp: skip unsubscribed guests, show send progress

Campaigns now go to every guest who has not unsubscribed in Mailchimp.
Unsubscribed, cleaned and archived guests are read from Mailchimp
first, left out, and never re-subscribed. A refused address no longer
cancels the whole send; it is left out and reported.

The "merge fields were invalid" refusals came from sending
skip_merge_validation in the request body. Mailchimp reads it from the
query string, so it is now sent there.

The send streams its progress, so the Campaigns page shows a progress
bar, the current step, a count of guests added and a timer. A new page,
Campaigns > Unsubscribed in Mailchimp, lists the guests who are left
out, with a CSV download.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LHbnzt849egZ8yN5Kkk57L
